(5187454, 752864, 68504, '<td valign="top">Mmm. Really like this, really like how you did it, and how many people can get 3 parallel power lines to LOOK parallel AND contribute to the scene... Sets the imagination free to savour the mood. (Congratulations to the unofficial award givers too.)</td>', 'Mmm. Really like this, really like how you did it, and how many people can get 3 parallel power lines to LOOK parallel AND contribute to the scene... Sets the imagination free to savour the mood. (Congratulations to the unofficial award givers too.)', '2009-01-12 15:26:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5187534, 752767, 53814, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> wonderful minimalism. And a perfect rim light on your ant, did you shoot him in a studio? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Lev, this was shot outdoors but I used a tripod and white board for fill, so it is almost a studio shot. I should have increased 1/2 stop for DOF. Thanks.</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: wonderful minimalism. And a perfect rim light on your ant, did you shoot him in a studio?   Lev, this was shot outdoors but I used a tripod and white board for fill, so it is almost a studio shot. I should have increased 1/2 stop for DOF. Thanks.', '2009-01-12 16:05:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5187567, 752767, 64670, '<td valign="top">Unbelievable!  SO good, good, GOOD!</td>', 'Unbelievable!  SO good, good, GOOD!', '2009-01-12 16:23:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5187583, 752677, 30364, '<td valign="top">Matt - I found one more pairing:  The "grumpy old man with the coffee" and the profile pic of <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=32767" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this guy.</a> <br/> <br/>And you say it was <strike>butthead</strike> pawdrix who pointed out the pairings?  Have you considered that he may be hiring actors to <i>stage</i> these elaborately improbable street tableaux that you photograph, without your actually being aware of it?<br/> <br/>"But why?", I hear you ask.  Who knows?  Who can say what madness romps unchecked through that tortured mind? I''ve read Anthony Bourdain; these chef guys are all very strange birds, and they do an awful lot of dope.</td>', 'Matt - I found one more pairing:  The "grumpy old man with the coffee" and the profile pic of this guy.  And you say it was butthead pawdrix who pointed out the pairings?  Have you considered that he may be hiring actors to stage these elaborately improbable street tableaux that you photograph, without your actually being aware of it? "But why?", I hear you ask.  Who knows?  Who can say what madness romps unchecked through that tortured mind? I''ve read Anthony Bourdain; these chef guys are all very strange birds, and they do an awful lot of dope.', '2009-01-12 16:36:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5187584, 753064, 53814, '<td valign="top">Great job Lev. Your processing choices are inspiring, you needed a special and unique eye to accomplish this placement.</td>', 'Great job Lev. Your processing choices are inspiring, you needed a special and unique eye to accomplish this placement.', '2009-01-12 16:36:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5187603, 753064, 28882, '<td valign="top">you shouldn''t feel embarrassed for your shot.  i think one of the key ingredients to being a good photographer is getting off your butt and putting yourself where you need to be.  great job!</td>', 'you shouldn''t feel embarrassed for your shot.  i think one of the key ingredients to being a good photographer is getting off your butt and putting yourself where you need to be.  great job!', '2009-01-12 16:59:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5187606, 752201, 66635, '<td valign="top">What an awesome photo!  Pacific Beach?</td>', 'What an awesome photo!  Pacific Beach?', '2009-01-12 17:00:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5187621, 753084, 83080, '<td valign="top">Nice job on this one.  I did a similar sand shot for a previous macro challenge &amp; really enjoyed seeing this done better than what I was able to accomplish:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=671307" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/849/120/671307.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/849/120/671307.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/849/120/671307.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Regarding the focus, sure the marble may be towards the front of the focal plane (very difficult to hit that same spot time after time), but I think the focus is fantastic since the marble and the stationary grains around it are quite sharp and the far part of the ejecta that is not on edge (the most important part imho) is going right through the center of the focal plane.<br/> <br/>Stopping the grains with a shorter flash might have been interesting, but I''m not sure I''d like that more than the texture you captured here with the sand''s motion blur.  I bet you have some very cool out takes from experimenting with the settings.<br/> <br/>Kudos to you Bob for having the perseverance to pull this shot off so well!  I think capturing sand drops makes water drops seem like an easy point and shoot.</td>', 'Nice job on this one.  I did a similar sand shot for a previous macro challenge & really enjoyed seeing this done better than what I was able to accomplish:  Regarding the focus, sure the marble may be towards the front of the focal plane (very difficult to hit that same spot time after time), but I think the focus is fantastic since the marble and the stationary grains around it are quite sharp and the far part of the ejecta that is not on edge (the most important part imho) is going right through the center of the focal plane. Stopping the grains with a shorter flash might have been interesting, but I''m not sure I''d like that more than the texture you captured here with the sand''s motion blur.  I bet you have some very cool out takes from experimenting with the settings. Kudos to you Bob for having the perseverance to pull this shot off so well!  I think capturing sand drops makes water drops seem like an easy point and shoot.', '2009-01-12 17:11:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5187636, 753026, 73235, '<td valign="top">Love your b/w conversion. increadibly dynamic</td>', 'Love your b/w conversion. increadibly dynamic', '2009-01-12 17:20:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5187668, 753064, 4793, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot</td>', 'Beautiful shot', '2009-01-12 17:32:03.000000', NULL, 0),
