(5197752, 753026, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LydiaToo:</b></div><hr/><i> Have you begun sharpening more than you used to, Irene?   It seems that lately my inner comment is "seems oversharpened" on your images before I even know they''re yours.<br/> <br/>I know I''m a nobody and you''re a great photographer... no really, you are... but still... I say it... and I thought you''d want to know. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Lydia, you''re hardly a nobody! Thanks for letting me know. I don''t think I''m sharpening more but I''ll keep it in mind.<br/>((Hugs))</td>', 'Originally posted by LydiaToo: Have you begun sharpening more than you used to, Irene?   It seems that lately my inner comment is "seems oversharpened" on your images before I even know they''re yours. I know I''m a nobody and you''re a great photographer... no really, you are... but still... I say it... and I thought you''d want to know.  Lydia, you''re hardly a nobody! Thanks for letting me know. I don''t think I''m sharpening more but I''ll keep it in mind.((Hugs))', '2009-01-17 01:37:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5198256, 752462, 61679, '<td valign="top">I saw your request for a comment on Art''s 10,000th comment thread.  Here is my take.  First, the post processing on the cross (B&amp;W conversion, contrast) is nicely done.  Two things hurt your score.  First was the subject itself.  The sand is not the main focus of the image no matter what your title implies.  Plus, fun cheerful images score better than this type of image.  Second, the background is extremely distracting.  If you cropped out the top 1/2 to 2/3 of the image (giving it a landscape orientation instead of portrait), the size and placement of the cross makes for a stronger composition. <br/> <br/>Tim</td>', 'I saw your request for a comment on Art''s 10,000th comment thread.  Here is my take.  First, the post processing on the cross (B&W conversion, contrast) is nicely done.  Two things hurt your score.  First was the subject itself.  The sand is not the main focus of the image no matter what your title implies.  Plus, fun cheerful images score better than this type of image.  Second, the background is extremely distracting.  If you cropped out the top 1/2 to 2/3 of the image (giving it a landscape orientation instead of portrait), the size and placement of the cross makes for a stronger composition.  Tim', '2009-01-17 09:59:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5198696, 752269, 30454, '<td valign="top">This one is also great in the series. I didn''t like sepia colors though compared the the first one. Excellent DOF.</td>', 'This one is also great in the series. I didn''t like sepia colors though compared the the first one. Excellent DOF.', '2009-01-17 11:13:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5198715, 752269, 55838, '<td valign="top">Just stumbled upon this when looking at another entry in the sand challenge.  I didn''t vote in this challenge but would have voted this high.  I love that it''s different and the DOF is wonderful.  Precious little sandy toesies were captured beautifully...makes me feel the texture of the pudgy little warm toes and the course cool sand.  Nice.</td>', 'Just stumbled upon this when looking at another entry in the sand challenge.  I didn''t vote in this challenge but would have voted this high.  I love that it''s different and the DOF is wonderful.  Precious little sandy toesies were captured beautifully...makes me feel the texture of the pudgy little warm toes and the course cool sand.  Nice.', '2009-01-17 11:19:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5198734, 753185, 55838, '<td valign="top">Great shot....very emotional.  From just a straight composition point of view, I like the patterns, contrast and the shadows are great.  Edit: just noticed this is your new personal best...congratulations!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-01-17 11:24:16.</i></td>', 'Great shot....very emotional.  From just a straight composition point of view, I like the patterns, contrast and the shadows are great.  Edit: just noticed this is your new personal best...congratulations!!', '2009-01-17 11:23:34.000000', '2009-01-17 11:24:16.000000', 0),
(5198743, 752824, 55838, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot.  I think this should have scored better...maybe it would have with a landscape orientation to make it feel bigger?  Who knows.  It''s lovely.  Edit: just noticed this is your new personal best...CONGRATULATIONS!!  (still...should''ve been higher IMO  : )<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-01-17 11:26:48.</i></td>', 'Very nice shot.  I think this should have scored better...maybe it would have with a landscape orientation to make it feel bigger?  Who knows.  It''s lovely.  Edit: just noticed this is your new personal best...CONGRATULATIONS!!  (still...should''ve been higher IMO  : )', '2009-01-17 11:25:52.000000', '2009-01-17 11:26:48.000000', 0),
(5198762, 753191, 55838, '<td valign="top">Great perspective and fantastic colors.  Congrats on top 20!</td>', 'Great perspective and fantastic colors.  Congrats on top 20!', '2009-01-17 11:30:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5199023, 751127, 3540, '<td valign="top">MsAmbrosia - I really like this photo.  Its not a photo that is going to stick in my mind for decades, but I''ll be reminded of it now and again.  Its hard to critique a photo like this as I don''t really find anything I would change dramatically.  The foreground is a little bit dark.  As opposed the obvious fix, lighten up the foreground a little, I''d be more inclined to pan back a little and sort of vignette the photo with the burn tool.  That''s really very minor and either way, I don''t think it effects the great mood of the photo.  I think you''ve done a fine job with it.  I think its a 6+ photo that was somewhat under appreciated due to the gloominess of shot.  Its a good photo.  Good Luck with your future endeavors - Bob</td>', 'MsAmbrosia - I really like this photo.  Its not a photo that is going to stick in my mind for decades, but I''ll be reminded of it now and again.  Its hard to critique a photo like this as I don''t really find anything I would change dramatically.  The foreground is a little bit dark.  As opposed the obvious fix, lighten up the foreground a little, I''d be more inclined to pan back a little and sort of vignette the photo with the burn tool.  That''s really very minor and either way, I don''t think it effects the great mood of the photo.  I think you''ve done a fine job with it.  I think its a 6+ photo that was somewhat under appreciated due to the gloominess of shot.  Its a good photo.  Good Luck with your future endeavors - Bob', '2009-01-17 12:55:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5199069, 753205, 3540, '<td valign="top">Pelle - Nice photo.  Maybe you should critique my work.  Its a very nice photo.  There are a couple things that really make it stand out to me.  The length of the shadow is great, very symbolic of the end of the day.  And I really like the contours of the sand.  That it shows no sky is really cool.  I think overall for the shot, it probably helped the EV.  There are a couple of "warmer" spots on the road, but nothing really hot.  The only suggestion I could possibly offer would be to crop it in a little tighter, but just to make the photo a little longer.  I don''t think it needs it at all.  You did really well with this.  Congrats on a great shot.  Sorry I have nothing to offer.  If you take some suckier photos, I can probably help more with those.  Keep up the good work - Bob</td>', 'Pelle - Nice photo.  Maybe you should critique my work.  Its a very nice photo.  There are a couple things that really make it stand out to me.  The length of the shadow is great, very symbolic of the end of the day.  And I really like the contours of the sand.  That it shows no sky is really cool.  I think overall for the shot, it probably helped the EV.  There are a couple of "warmer" spots on the road, but nothing really hot.  The only suggestion I could possibly offer would be to crop it in a little tighter, but just to make the photo a little longer.  I don''t think it needs it at all.  You did really well with this.  Congrats on a great shot.  Sorry I have nothing to offer.  If you take some suckier photos, I can probably help more with those.  Keep up the good work - Bob', '2009-01-17 13:05:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5199671, 752269, 70514, '<td valign="top">Seems this should''ve scored higher, but hey, what do I know?  Love the simplicity of the hands and feet - adds to the story, imo.</td>', 'Seems this should''ve scored higher, but hey, what do I know?  Love the simplicity of the hands and feet - adds to the story, imo.', '2009-01-17 15:52:32.000000', NULL, 0),
